cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite the versioned software release."
title: "Genuine Zero Uniform Atlas Energy"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Massensini
    given-names: Thiago
license: MIT
version: 0.15.0
date-released: 2026-08-19
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of the native real-camera/Genuine zero identity, the
  faithful C2--C7 cutoff operator, exact critical cutoff-tail jets, and the
  finite-to-limit transverse-energy architecture. Version 0.15.0 completes
  the quantitative second-jet gate: the M^(-3/2) log(M)^2 derivative-tail
  rate is absorbed into fixed camerawise C_b(t)/M constants, the complete
  six-camera finite second jet receives a cutoff-independent bound, both
  finite curvature coordinates receive fixed C_curv(t)/M estimates, and the
  local Schur ledger no longer accepts an external secondJetBound hypothesis.
  The derivative analysis uses no supplied height and does not require
  simplicity; the later quadratic coercivity route remains the
  multiplicity-one sector. The release does not promote the remaining
  denominator floors, non-jet C/M constants, compact-region coverage,
  numerical evidence, or readout-domain equivalences to an unconditional
  confinement theorem.
